# This file is published to the gh-pages branch as part of every deploy.
#
# The gh-pages branch holds only the built site. If it ever gets checked out
# in a normal working tree, everything else in that directory - dependencies,
# build output and, critically, the .env holding Zoho credentials - shows up
# as untouched by any ignore rule and can be staged by a stray `git add -A`.
# These rules make that mistake impossible on this branch too.
#
# It lives in public/ rather than being committed to gh-pages directly because
# `gh-pages -d dist` wipes the branch on each deploy; publishing it as part of
# dist/ is what makes it stick.

.env
.env.*
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.vite/
coverage/
*.log
src/
